  "text": "Defences that actually hold Ordered by how much they are worth. The first three are architecture; the rest reduce noise. Flow Defence in depth, strongest first Replay 1 Least privilege on the tools The agent can only do what its tools allow. A read-only agent cannot be talked into a write. This is the one defence that holds no matter what the model does. 2 Identity from the session, never the model Scope every query by the authenticated user in code. If the model supplies the customer id, the model can be persuaded to supply a different one. 3 Human confirmation on irreversible actions Sending, paying, deleting, publishing. A person approving the specific action, seeing what it actually is —"
