  "section": "Why a developer should care about this",
  "text": "Why a developer should care about this Governance sounds like somebody else s job legal s, compliance s, a committee s. It arrives as your problem for a simple reason: the obligations attach to the system, and you are the one who knows what the system does. Nobody else can tell an auditor what data went into the retrieval index or what the model is allowed to act on. In plain English Governance is the paperwork that proves you were careful, and the process that makes you actually be careful. Most of it is not a legal question at all it is writing down what the system does, what it must not do, who decided that, and how you would know if it stopped being true. i The good news: if you have don"
