  "section": "Risk tiers: the idea behind every framework",
  "text": "Risk tiers: the idea behind every framework Regulations differ in detail and agree on the core move: obligations scale with potential harm, not with technical sophistication. A model deciding what music to play and a model deciding who gets a loan are treated very differently, however similar the code. Figure The shape every framework shares ! The tier is set by the use case, not the technology. The same model, the same prompt and the same code can be minimal risk in one product and high risk in another. A CV summariser is a summariser; a CV summariser that ranks candidates influences employment decisions and is a different regulatory object entirely."
